* ============================================================================
* Datasheet-fitted BJT models  (ME5120 bench-supply project)
* Fitted by Claude to the manufacturer datasheet numbers below; not vendor
* models. Re-check against the datasheet if a parameter is changed.
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TIP3055DS - onsemi TIP3055 (TO-247), same die as 2N3055 [DS2 p.2 note]
*   hFE 20 min / 70 max at IC = 4 A, VCE = 4 V   [DS2 p.2]   -> model ~28 at 4 A, ~52 at 1 A
*   VBE(on) 1.8 V max at IC = 4 A                [DS2 p.2]   -> model ~1.0 V at 4 A, 0.72 V at 1 A
*   fT 2.5 MHz min                               [DS2 p.2]   -> TF = 55 ns
* BC547BDS - onsemi/Fairchild BC547B
*   hFE 200-450 (B group) at IC = 2 mA           [DS3 p.1]   -> model ~300
*   VBE(on) 0.58 / 0.66 / 0.70 V at 2 mA, 5 V    [DS3 p.1]   -> model 0.659 V
* ============================================================================
.model TIP3055DS NPN(IS=1e-11 BF=70 NF=1 IKF=2.5 ISE=1e-11 NE=1.6 VAF=100 RB=0.8 RE=0.04 RC=0.08 CJE=600p CJC=250p TF=55n BR=5)
.model BC547BDS  NPN(IS=1.8e-14 BF=290 NF=1 IKF=0.15 VAF=60 RB=10 RE=0.6 RC=0.5 ISE=2e-14 NE=1.6 CJE=12p CJC=4p TF=0.4n BR=7)
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BC557BDS - PNP complement of BC547B (BC556/557/558 family), used as the
*   constant-current source for the adjustable current limit (SIM05).
*   Parameters mirror BC547BDS: hFE ~300, VBE(on) ~0.66 V at 2 mA.  (datasheet DS4 to be added)
* D1N4148  - 1N4148 small-signal diode (widely used SPICE parameters, as in
*   LTspice's standard diode library). VF ~0.62 V at 1 mA.          (datasheet DS5 to be added)
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.model BC557BDS  PNP(IS=1.8e-14 BF=290 NF=1 IKF=0.15 VAF=60 RB=10 RE=0.6 RC=0.5 ISE=2e-14 NE=1.6 CJE=12p CJC=6p TF=0.5n BR=7)
.model D1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 CJO=4p M=0.4 TT=20n BV=100 IBV=100u)
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TIP3055MIN - TIP3055DS with BF cut to 27 -> hFE ~20 at ~1 A: the datasheet
*   MINIMUM hFE (20 at 4 A) [DS2 p.2] applied at our current = worst case for base drive.
* BD139DS - BD139 medium-power NPN driver (TO-126), hFE ~130 at 50 mA
*   (BD139 datasheet DS6 to be added: hFE 40 min at 150 mA).
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.model TIP3055MIN NPN(IS=1e-11 BF=27 NF=1 IKF=2.5 ISE=1e-11 NE=1.6 VAF=100 RB=0.8 RE=0.04 RC=0.08 CJE=600p CJC=250p TF=55n BR=5)
.model BD139DS NPN(IS=2e-13 BF=160 NF=1 IKF=0.6 ISE=2e-13 NE=1.6 VAF=100 RB=2 RE=0.1 RC=0.2 CJE=150p CJC=40p TF=2n BR=5)
